---
import SourcePanel from "./SourcePanel.astro";

const { topic, next, compact = false } = Astro.props;
const facts = [
  ["Duration", "4.32 billion human years"],
  ["Contains", "14 Manvantaras"],
  ["Equivalent to", "1,000 Maha Yugas"],
  ["Current cycle", "Shveta Varaha Kalpa"],
];
const scales = [
  ["Human life", "About 100 years"],
  ["Kali Yuga", "432,000 years"],
  ["Maha Yuga", "4.32 million years"],
  ["Manvantara", "306.72 million years"],
  ["Kalpa", "4.32 billion years"],
];
---

<article class="kalpa-reading">
  <header>
    <p class="eyebrow">Selected layer - Kalpa</p>
    <h1>One Day of Brahma</h1>
    <p class="lead">A Kalpa is one complete daytime cycle of Brahma in the traditional Puranic model of cosmic time. It is one of the largest recurring units used to describe the unfolding of the universe.</p>
    <p>To a human being, a century feels long. To a civilization, a thousand years may feel significant. A Kalpa stretches across <strong>4.32 billion years</strong>.</p>
    <p>Within that span, worlds emerge, life evolves, countless generations pass, and cosmic history unfolds through vast repeating cycles. A Kalpa is not merely a number. It is a complete chapter in the life of the universe.</p>
  </header>

  <dl class="facts">
    {facts.map(([label, value]) => <div><dt>{label}</dt><dd>{value}</dd></div>)}
  </dl>

  <div class="reading-body">
    <main>
      <section>
        <h2>What does a Kalpa explain?</h2>
        <p>A Kalpa provides the larger frame for understanding recurring periods of cosmic activity and rest in the traditional Puranic model.</p>
        <p>It places smaller cycles such as Manvantaras, Maha Yugas, and the Four Yugas within one vast daytime cycle of Brahma.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How a Kalpa is organized</h2>
        <p>A Kalpa is not a single uninterrupted period. It contains fourteen Manvantaras and is equivalent to one thousand Maha Yugas.</p>
        <p>Each smaller layer gives a more detailed view of where events and ages belong within the larger cosmic cycle.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>

  <details class="full-guide" open={!compact} data-compact={compact || undefined}>
    <summary><span>Continue reading</span><b>Read full Kalpa guide</b></summary>
    <div class="reading-body">
      <main>
      <section>
        <h2>The current Kalpa</h2>
        <p>Traditional sources identify the present cosmic cycle as the <strong>Shveta Varaha Kalpa</strong>. The name is associated with the Varaha incarnation of Vishnu.</p>
        <p>In the traditional narrative, the Earth had become submerged within the cosmic waters. Vishnu, in the form of Varaha, restores and raises the Earth so creation can continue. The account symbolizes renewal, restoration, and the re-establishment of cosmic order.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The beginning of a Kalpa</h2>
        <p>According to traditional cosmology, a period of rest follows the previous cosmic cycle. The universe remains in an unmanifest state, awaiting the next cycle of creation.</p>
        <p>Then a new Kalpa begins. Brahma awakens, creation resumes, the worlds become active, cosmic order is established, and beings emerge into existence. This marks the dawn of another vast cosmic cycle.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The fourteen Manvantaras</h2>
        <p>Each Manvantara represents a major chapter within the larger cosmic cycle. Together, the fourteen Manvantaras form a framework through which life, civilizations, sages, and cosmic events unfold across a Kalpa.</p>
        <aside class="note">
          <p class="eyebrow">Our current position</p>
          <p>We are described as living within the <strong>Shveta Varaha Kalpa</strong>, the <strong>7th Manvantara</strong>, the <strong>28th Maha Yuga</strong>, and specifically within <strong>Kali Yuga</strong>.</p>
        </aside>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>A day and night of Brahma</h2>
        <p>A Kalpa represents only the daytime of Brahma. An equally long night follows it. During the day, creation remains active. During the night, creation enters a dormant state. When the next day begins, creation resumes.</p>
        <div class="comparison">
          <div><span>Day of Brahma</span><strong>4.32 billion years</strong><small>Creation remains active</small></div>
          <div><span>Night of Brahma</span><strong>4.32 billion years</strong><small>Creation enters rest</small></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Major events of a Kalpa</h2>
        <ol class="events">
          <li><strong>Dawn of creation</strong><span>A new Kalpa begins and the universe becomes active once again.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Restoration of cosmic order</strong><span>The current Kalpa is associated with Varaha and the restoration of the Earth.</span></li>
          <li><strong>The fourteen Manvantaras</strong><span>The Kalpa progresses through fourteen major chapters.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Cosmic rest</strong><span>Creation gradually prepares for withdrawal and rest.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Transition to the next cycle</strong><span>The end of one Kalpa prepares the beginning of another.</span></li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The end of a Kalpa</h2>
        <p>At the conclusion of a Kalpa, a partial cosmic dissolution occurs. This event is traditionally known as <strong>Naimittika Pralaya</strong>.</p>
        <p>The active universe gradually withdraws, ordinary activity ceases in lower realms, and creation enters a state of rest. This is not the end of existence itself. It is a pause between cycles and preparation for renewal.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>The scale of a Kalpa</h2>
        <div class="scale-list">{scales.map(([label, value]) => <div><span>{label}</span><strong>{value}</strong></div>)}</div>
        <p>At this scale, civilizations become brief moments. Empires rise and disappear, languages emerge and vanish, species evolve and become extinct, and even geological ages occupy only a fraction of a Kalpa.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What a Kalpa teaches</h2>
        <p>The idea of a Kalpa is not only about measuring time. It also offers a way of understanding existence.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Time operates on many scales.</li>
          <li>Creation is cyclical rather than linear.</li>
          <li>Endings can prepare new beginnings.</li>
          <li>Individual lives exist within much larger patterns.</li>
          <li>Change is a fundamental feature of the cosmos.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Through the lens of a Kalpa, human history becomes part of a much larger story and ordinary life can be viewed from a cosmic perspective.</p>
      </section>

    </main>

    <SourcePanel sources={topic.data.sources} sourceNote={topic.data.sourceNote} traditionNote={topic.data.traditionNote} reviewedBy={topic.data.reviewedBy} lastReviewed={topic.data.lastReviewed} contentVersion={topic.data.contentVersion} />

  </details>

  <a class="continue" href={`/atlas/${next?.slug ?? "manvantara"}`}>
    <span><small>Ready to move deeper?</small><strong>Next: {next?.title ?? "Manvantara"}</strong><em>Discover the great chapters that unfold within a Kalpa.</em></span>
    <b>Explore next layer -></b>
  </a>
</article>

<style>
  .kalpa-reading { color:#eee3cf; }
  header,.reading-body,.facts,.kalpa-reading :global(.source-panel),.continue,.full-guide > summary { width:min(100% - 2rem,72rem); margin-inline:auto; }
  header { padding:clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem) 0 2.5rem; }
  header p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width:62ch; color:#b3aca1; line-height:1.85; }
  header strong,.reading-body strong { color:#e9b65f; font-weight:650; }
  h1,h2 { font-family:var(--serif); font-weight:400; letter-spacing:-.025em; }
  h1 { max-width:15ch; margin:.35rem 0 1rem; font-size:clamp(3.2rem,6vw,6rem); line-height:1; }
  .lead { color:#d0c5b3 !important; font-size:clamp(1.08rem,1.5vw,1.3rem); }
  .facts { display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); border-block:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18); }
  .facts div { padding:1rem; }
  .facts div + div { border-left:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14); }
  dt { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  dd { margin:.25rem 0 0; color:#e5dac8; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.05rem; }
  .reading-body { padding-block:2rem; }
  main { width:min(100%,46rem); }
  section { border-bottom:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14); padding-block:2rem; }
  h2 { margin:0 0 .8rem; font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,2.6rem); line-height:1.15; }
  section p,section li { color:#aaa49a; line-height:1.85; }
  section p { margin:.65rem 0 0; }
  .note { margin:1.5rem 0 0; border-left:2px solid #e9b65f; padding:.2rem 0 .2rem 1rem; }
  .note p { margin:.25rem 0; color:#c2b9aa; }
  .comparison { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:.7rem; margin-top:1.5rem; }
  .comparison div { border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.16); border-radius:.7rem; padding:1rem; }
  .comparison span,.comparison strong,.comparison small { display:block; }
  .comparison span,.comparison small { color:#99938a; font-size:.68rem; }
  .comparison strong { margin:.25rem 0; font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.15rem; font-weight:500; }
  .events { margin:1.2rem 0 0; padding:0; list-style:none; counter-reset:event; }
  .events li { display:grid; grid-template-columns:2rem 1fr; gap:0 .7rem; padding:.8rem 0; border-top:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.1); counter-increment:event; }
  .events li::before { grid-row:1/3; color:#e9b65f; font-size:.7rem; content:"0" counter(event); }
  .events strong,.events span { display:block; }.events strong{color:#ddd2c0}.events span{font-size:.85rem}
  .scale-list { margin-top:1.25rem; border-block:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14); }
  .scale-list div { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; padding:.65rem 0; border-bottom:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.08); }
  .scale-list span { color:#aaa49a; }.scale-list strong{font-size:.9rem}
  ul { padding-left:1.15rem; }
  .references { border-bottom:0; }
  .full-guide { border:0; }
  .full-guide:not([data-compact]) > summary { display:none; }
  .full-guide > summary { display:flex; width:fit-content; align-items:center; gap:.55rem; margin-top:.9rem; border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.24); border-radius:999px; padding:.55rem .8rem; background:rgb(233 182 95/.035); color:#e9b65f; cursor:pointer; list-style:none; }
  .full-guide > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display:none; }
  .full-guide > summary span { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.08em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .full-guide > summary b { font-size:.67rem; }
  .full-guide[open] > summary b { font-size:0; }
  .full-guide[open] > summary b::after { font-size:.67rem; content:"Hide full guide"; }
  .full-guide[open] > .reading-body { animation:guide-reveal 420ms ease both; }
  .continue { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; gap:1rem; margin-top:2rem; border:1px solid rgb(101 215 220/.22); border-radius:1rem; padding:1.2rem 1.35rem; background:linear-gradient(100deg,rgb(101 215 220/.055),transparent); color:#65d7dc; }
  .continue span > * { display:block; }
  .continue small { color:#99938a; font-size:.62rem; letter-spacing:.1em; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .continue strong { font-family:var(--serif); font-size:1.7rem; font-weight:400; }
  .continue em { color:#aaa49a; font-size:.72rem; font-style:normal; }
  .continue b { font-size:.68rem; text-transform:uppercase; }
  .kalpa-reading{border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.2);border-radius:1.4rem;padding-bottom:1rem;background:linear-gradient(145deg,rgb(10 27 36/.72),rgb(3 13 20/.48));box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.035),0 24px 80px rgb(0 0 0/.22);backdrop-filter:blur(20px) saturate(115%)}
  .facts{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.18);border-radius:1rem;background:rgb(255 255 255/.025);box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025);backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}
  .note{border:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.17);border-left:2px solid #e9b65f;border-radius:.7rem;padding:.8rem 1rem;background:rgb(233 182 95/.035);backdrop-filter:blur(12px)}
  .comparison div,.continue,.full-guide>summary{box-shadow:inset 0 1px rgb(255 255 255/.025);backdrop-filter:blur(14px)}
  @keyframes guide-reveal { from { opacity:0; transform:translateY(-8px) } to { opacity:1; transform:none } }
  @media(max-width:800px){
    .facts{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.facts div:nth-child(odd){border-left:0}.facts div:nth-child(n+3){border-top:1px solid rgb(233 182 95/.14)}
    .comparison{grid-template-columns:1fr}.continue{align-items:flex-end}
  }
</style>
